redesign.problem:
Option (a), today's design, needs 524 lines of say.ts:
- a CLAIMS table of Spanish regexes (say.ts:115-185) that grows with each wording change and depends on render.ts wording (say.ts:107-113);
- a restates/FILLER filter (say.ts:290-311);
- the check run twice with different sources: in the loop for repair (loop.ts:199-232) and in execute for the final drop (say.ts:466-524);
- per-tool special cases: set_reminder text is always dropped (say.ts:498-501, prompt.ts:189), yet the field is still in the schema.

The payoff, from my count of the 2026-11-22T03-43 all-split run (182 scenarios, 195 turns), was 6 texts on action tools:
- 3 dropped: s076, s170, and one delete;
- 2 sent as pure restatement that slipped past `restates`: s169 and s182 ("Anotado: el sueldo te cae el 28." beside "🧠 Me acuerdo: sueldo: me cae el 28");
- 1 useful: s012 "¿Fue $15 o te faltan ceros?".

Three earlier all-split runs look the same (about 22 texts in about 760 turns, about half dropped).

The repair turn this path causes shows up as a second-turn cause in every measured run (agent-spec.md:944, 997, 1143: "repaired text 1"). Each one costs about 1.5 s.

redesign.proposal:
Tool shapes:
```ts
reply: { text: z.string().max(280) }          // alone: true
skip:  { part: z.string().max(80), reason: z.enum(['not_found','what_to_change','cannot','separately']) }
// code renders: "No encontré {part}." / "¿Qué querés cambiar de {part}?" / "{Part}: eso no lo puedo hacer." / "Mandame {part} aparte."
```

`skip.part` is checked structurally: at most 8 words, and every folded word must appear in the message or the evidence lines (list, found rows, window). No claim or number regexes are needed for it.

`reply` is alone, so `Applied` is always empty. The claim check reduces to proof from the window, and the `kind` field of each CLAIMS entry is deleted. The numbers check runs once, in the loop, with every source. execute just appends the verdict and drops nothing.

The one capability lost is s012's question about a low-confidence amount. Code already marks that movement `(?)` from the typed `confidence`. If the owner wants the question, it becomes a fixed code line on `confidence:'low'`.

Deleted:
- in say.ts: Applied, KIND_OF_TOOL, restates/FILLER, the per-action composeReply loop, the set_reminder special case;
- in loop.ts: amountsOf (11-23), the Applied build (205-216), REPAIR_OTHER;
- execute.ts:110-120, where the texts are collected;
- the `text` rules in prompt.ts:33, 139-141 and 144.

Option (c) is rejected: a model-written record can name the wrong movement with a number that passes the check (agent-spec.md:260-263), it breaks the owner's "code renders every record", and the brief notes Haiku leaks reasoning-like text when thinking is off.

redesign.measure:
Run the scenario dev split twice, then test once.

It must show:
- at least 95% fully right, 0 silent wrong changes, 0 invented numbers;
- multi-action 16/16 and the "part not done" scenarios passing (the `No encontré el súper` one, s096);
- the second-turn rate equal or lower (the repaired-text cause should go to 0).

Reject if:
- any scenario loses a part silently;
- `skip` part refusals happen more than once per run;
- the second-turn rate rises by more than 2 points;
- s012, s169 or s182 regress on grade.

Run the scenario dev split, with s061 repeated 10 times.

Reject if:
- s061 passes fewer than its baseline 6 of 10;
- unnecessary questions rise;
- the rejected `ask_user` shape count goes above baseline.

redesign.problem:
The strict-era shapes stay, even though the file says the limits are gone (schema.ts:62-69):
- `Say()` nullable-default-null;
- RangeSchema `month/year: default(0)` and `from/to: default('')` (schema.ts:110-121);
- `other` as a mini-language string parsed by `parseOther` (schema.ts:173-178, range.ts:295-331);
- `forget_fact` with id 0 / key '' sentinels (schema.ts:201-202, tools.ts:24);
- summarize filters nullable-default-null.

MCP inherits them through `.extend()`, so a client is told "a field a period does not use stays 0 or \"\"" (mcp/tools.ts:351).

The factory pattern (schema.ts:57) is stale. I ran `z.toJSONSchema` on Zod 4.6.7 with one reused enum or object instance and a discriminated union: the output is inlined, `has $defs: false`.

redesign.measure:
Run `count_tokens` and the scenario dev split.

Reject if:
- refused-for-shape calls (`invalid input:` in the audit) rise above the baseline of about 1 per run;
- the summary or time-reference tags drop more than 1 scenario;
- the second-turn rate rises.

Factories alone can land with no eval: the JSON bytes are identical, so assert that `TOOLS` is byte-equal.

redesign.problem:
execute.ts:122-213 and mcp/write.ts:183-346 each switch over the same Outcome and call the same renderers (renderLog, renderCorrection, renderDeletion, renderUndo, renderRemembered, renderForgot). Both compute the same status string separately:
- execute's `steps.outcome` (execute.ts:138-210);
- MCP's `status`;
- render.ts:356-375, where `reminderReply` returns an `outcome` string.

The MCP path also re-queries rows that applyCall had just written (write.ts:201 and :226 `rowsByIds`). That keeps its presenter impure.

Outcome overloads `kind`. The remember_fact variant carries `kind: FactKind` (apply.ts:78), while every other variant uses `kind` for 'applied'/'gone'.

redesign.proposal:
`src/es.ts` (pure) holds: `MONTHS`, `MONTHS_SHORT`, `WEEKDAY: Record<Weekday, { one; many }>`, `weekdayOf(iso)`, `money(amount, currency)` (moved from render.ts:127), `day(iso, today)` → 'hoy'|'ayer'|'dd/mm'|'dd/mm/yy', `clock(at)`, `list(items)` ("a, b y c") and `count(n, one, many)`.

Then:
- time.ts keeps only calendar arithmetic;
- render.ts, render-summary.ts and describe.ts import from es.ts;
- MCP keeps its English field descriptions;
- the record strings it embeds come from es.ts.

Pick one date format, the padded `dd/mm[/yy]`. say.ts's tokenizer reads both, so nothing breaks.

In understand.ts (council 1):

interface Shown { today; time; now; movements; facts; factsTotal; reminders; sent; turns; pending; quoted; history: 'none'|'complete'|'more' }
renderContext(shown, message: { text, photo?, voice? }): string
allowed(shown): { movements: Set<number>; facts: Set<number>; reminders: Set<number>; sole?: number }
quotable(shown, found?): string[]

Each entity has one describe(x); the context prints `id=${x.id} ${describe(x)}` and the numbers check reads describe(x). runAgent takes `shown` instead of ten loose fields.
